            <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">No credit card required • Personalized Roadmap</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem (Blocks of Text for SEO) -->
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
                <h2 class="section-title text-center mb-8" style="font-size: 2.5rem;">Why Success Feels Like a Trap</h2>
                <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                    <h3 style="color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">The "Chief Everything Officer" Problem</h3>
                    <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                        Most founders reach $1M-$3M in revenue through sheer force of will. You are the best salesperson, the best project manager, and the final quality check. This works—until it doesn't. 
                    </p>
                    <p style="color: #ccc;">
                        As you scale, the complexity of your business outpaces your personal capacity. You become the bottleneck. Every new client adds stress, not freedom. This is the "Scaling Trap."
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="grid-3">
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>❌ The Golden Handcuffs</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You make good money, but you can't leave for a week without things breaking.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>❌ Profit Compression</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You hire more people to help, but efficiency drops and margins get thinner.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card">
                        <h3>❌ The Plateau</h3>
                        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You've been stuck at the same revenue level for 12+ months despite working harder.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 1: Paid Acquisition -->
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">Paid Acquisition Engine</h2>
            <p class="price text-center">$2,250<span class="price-sub">/month</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: You're Trapped in the Referral Hamster Wheel</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    Referrals are great—until they're not. Your growth is completely at the mercy of your existing client's schedules and moods. One bad quarter? Your pipeline dries up. You can't forecast. You can't plan hires. You're constantly white-knuckling it, hoping someone sends business your way.
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    Most founders try running ads themselves. They burn $10k in 30 days with zero ROI, then swear off paid acquisition forever. The truth? Ads work. But only when someone obsessively manages them every single day—which you don't have time to do.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: A Predictable Lead Machine</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We build and manage a self-sustaining acquisition system that turns $1 into $5. Every day, we're optimizing your ad spend, killing underperformers, and scaling winners. You wake up to qualified leads in your inbox—not because you got lucky with a referral, but because you have a machine that runs 24/7.
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>Daily Ads Management</strong> - We monitor performance hourly, not monthly</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Creative Testing</strong> - New ad angles every week to beat fatigue</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Multi-Platform Scaling</strong> - Google, Facebook, LinkedIn—wherever your buyers are</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>ROI Dashboards</strong> - Real-time tracking so you know exactly what's working</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05); border-color: var(--primary);">
                <p style="color: #ccc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic;">
                    "We went from 2-3 inbound leads per month to 40+ qualified SQLs. For the first time in 5 years, I can actually forecast revenue." - Agency Owner, $2.8M ARR
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 2: Funnel Architecture -->
    <section class="section" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">Funnel Architecture</h2>
            <p class="price text-center">$3,500<span class="price-sub">/project</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: Traffic Doesn't Equal Revenue</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    You're driving traffic to your site. People are clicking. And then... nothing. They bounce. They ghost. Your sales team is stuck chasing lukewarm leads who "need to think about it." Why? Because your funnel is a leaky bucket. There's no qualification, no nurture, no reason for them to act *now*.
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    Most founders slap together a landing page and pray. But high-converting funnels are psychological warfare. Every word, every button, every step is engineered to move prospects from curious to committed. You don't have time to A/B test copy for 6 months. We do.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: A Funnel That Qualifies & Converts On Autopilot</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We design, build, and optimize complete sales funnels that do the heavy lifting for you. From the first ad click to the booked call, every step is optimized to filter out tire-kickers and fast-track serious buyers. Your sales team only talks to people who are ready to buy—not "just browsing."
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>Conversion Copywriting</strong> - Psychology-backed messaging that resonates with your ICP</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>UX/UI Design</strong> - Clean, fast, mobile-optimized pages that don't look like 2015</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Technical Integration</strong> - CRM, email, SMS, Calendly—everything talks to each other</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>A/B Testing Setup</strong> - Continuous optimization to improve conversion rates month over month</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05); border-color: var(--primary);">
                <p style="color: #ccc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic;">
                    "Our funnel went from 8% conversion to 31% in 60 days. Same traffic, 4x the bookings. This paid for itself in week one." - SaaS Founder, $1.2M ARR
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 3: CRM Automation -->
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">CRM Transformation</h2>
            <p class="price text-center">$2,500<span class="price-sub">/setup</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: Your CRM is a Digital Junk Drawer</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    Be honest: when was the last time your CRM actually *helped* you close a deal? Right now, it's just a contact graveyard. Leads fall through the cracks. Your team forgets to follow up. Deals sit in "Proposal Sent" for 90 days because no one knows who's supposed to do what.
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    You're manually entering data. Manually sending follow-up emails. Manually updating deal stages. It's 2026, and you're still running a 1990s sales process. Every hour your team spends on admin is an hour they're not closing revenue.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: A Self-Driving CRM</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We turn your CRM from a glorified Rolodex into a revenue machine. Leads are automatically enriched, scored, and routed. Follow-ups happen on autopilot. Contracts get sent at the perfect time. Your sales team stops doing data entry and starts closing deals. You finally have visibility into your entire pipeline—without asking anyone for updates.
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>Custom Pipelines</strong> - Stages that match your actual sales process, not HubSpot's defaults</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Auto-Follow Up</strong> - Email & SMS sequences triggered by behavior, not manual clicks</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Contract Automation</strong> - Proposals and agreements sent automatically when deals hit "Qualified"</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Lead Scoring</strong> - AI-powered prioritization so your team calls the hottest leads first</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05); border-color: var(--primary);">
                <p style="color: #ccc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic;">
                    "We cut our sales cycle from 45 days to 18 days. Our close rate doubled because nothing falls through the cracks anymore." - B2B SaaS VP of Sales
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 4: Data & Analytics -->
    <section class="section" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">Data & Attribution</h2>
            <p class="price text-center">$1,500<span class="price-sub">/month</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: You're Flying Blind</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    Quick question: which marketing channel drove your last 3 deals? If you can't answer that in 5 seconds, you're guessing. And guessing is expensive. You're probably over-investing in channels that don't convert and under-investing in the ones that print money.
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    Your Google Analytics shows "traffic." Your CRM shows "deals closed." But there's a dark void in between where attribution goes to die. iOS updates killed cookie tracking. Your ads manager says one thing, your revenue dashboard says another. You have no idea what's actually working.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: Total Revenue Visibility</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We implement server-side tracking that survives iOS updates and ad blockers. You'll know exactly which dollar of ad spend generated which dollar of revenue. Multi-touch attribution shows you the full customer journey—from first click to closed deal. No more guessing. Just data-driven decisions that compound over time.
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>Server-Side Tracking</strong> - Bulletproof data that can't be blocked by browsers</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Multi-Touch Attribution</strong> - See the entire customer journey, not just "last click"</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Live Looker Studio Dashboards</strong> - Real-time revenue data, no Excel gymnastics</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Conversion API Setup</strong> - Feed clean data directly to Facebook & Google for better ad performance</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05); border-color: var(--primary);">
                <p style="color: #ccc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic;">
                    "We discovered LinkedIn was driving 60% of our revenue despite only getting 10% of our ad spend. Reallocated budget and 3x'd ROI in 90 days." - Agency Owner, $4M ARR
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 5: Content Engine -->
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">The Authority Engine</h2>
            <p class="price text-center">$4,000<span class="price-sub">/month</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: You're Invisible Where It Matters</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    Your buyers are on LinkedIn. Your competitors are on LinkedIn. Everyone's posting. But you? You're too busy running your business to "build a personal brand." So prospects go with the founder who *seems* like the expert—even if their product is worse than yours.
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    Content is not optional anymore. Companies that dominate their categories have omnipresent founders. They're in your inbox, your feed, your podcast app. You know them, trust them, and buy from them. Meanwhile, you're a ghost. And ghosts don't win deals.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: Omnipresent Authority, On Autopilot</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We handle the entire content engine. You record one 30-minute Loom per week. We turn it into 50+ assets: LinkedIn posts, newsletter issues, video clips, Twitter threads, and carousels. You become the go-to expert in your space without spending 10 hours a week on "content creation." Leads start DMing you before you even run ads.
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>LinkedIn Ghostwriting</strong> - Daily posts that sound like you (because they're based on your voice memos)</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Newsletter Operations</strong> - Weekly emails that nurture your list into buyers</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Video Editing & Repurposing</strong> - Turn one video into 20 short clips optimized for each platform</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Multi-Platform Distribution</strong> - LinkedIn, Twitter, YouTube, email—everywhere your audience is</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.05); border-color: var(--primary);">
                <p style="color: #ccc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-style: italic;">
                    "I went from 2,000 LinkedIn followers to 18,000 in 6 months. Now I get 10-15 qualified DMs per week asking to work together. Zero outbound." - Consultant, $800K ARR
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Service 6: Full Retainer -->
    <section class="section" style="background: radial-gradient(circle at center, rgba(255,107,53,0.1) 0%, #050505 100%); border-top: 2px solid var(--primary);">
        <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <h2 class="text-center mb-4" style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--primary);">Full Growth Retainer</h2>
            <p class="price text-center" style="color: white;">$5,200<span class="price-sub">/week</span></p>
            
            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; border-color: var(--primary);">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: You Need a Team, Not Another Vendor</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    Hiring a Head of Growth costs $180K/year + equity. A marketing coordinator? $70K. A funnel designer? $90K. A paid ads specialist? $100K. You're looking at $400K+ just to build a competent growth team. And that assumes you hire perfectly on the first try (you won't).
                </p>
                <p style="color: #ccc;">
                    Or you could hire agencies. But agencies treat you like ticket #47. You're in a Slack channel with 10 other clients. They deliver cookie-cutter work and disappear when things go wrong. You need a team that cares about your business like it's theirs.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card" style="margin-top: 2rem; border-color: var(--primary);">
                <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--secondary);">The Solution: Your Entire Growth Team, On Demand</h3>
                <p style="color: #ccc; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    This is not a "service." It's a partnership. We embed directly into your Slack. We attend your team meetings. We execute on everything from ad creative to hiring your next sales rep. You get a full growth team (ads, funnels, CRM, content, analytics) for less than the cost of one senior hire. And we move fast—because we're not juggling 50 other clients.
                </p>
                <ul style="color: #ccc; list-style: none; line-height: 2;">
                    <li>→ <strong>Dedicated Growth Team</strong> - Strategist, designer, developer, copywriter, ads manager</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Unlimited Projects</strong> - No scope creep, no nickel-and-diming. If it drives growth, we do it.</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Weekly Strategy Calls</strong> - We don't wait for monthly check-ins. We move weekly.</li>
                    <li>→ <strong>Hiring & Training Support</strong> - We help you hire and onboard your internal growth team when you're ready</li>
                </ul>
